  "name": "A combat pet in a widened battleground bracket gains its own level-stat difference",
  "contract": "A level 12 Human Warlock with an Imp (416) who enters a Warsong Gulch of the 10-29 bracket gets a health-only lift. The Warlock gains the level 29 minus level 12 rows of player_class_stats in base health and Stamina: maximum health +333 (base health +223 and 11 Stamina x 10); mana is not lifted. The Imp gains the difference of its own pet_levelstats rows in base health (+407) and Stamina (+19), so its own Stamina gain is not counted twice; the 75% Stamina it inherits from the lifted owner adds at most 9 Stamina (health +490 in all). Its Strength, Agility and mana are not lifted. Output ratios are the lifted to own health: the Imp 591 / 184 = 3.21196 from pet_levelstats rows 416 at levels 29 and 12, and the Warlock (128 + 20 + 10 x 7 = 218 at level 12, 351 + 20 + 10 x 18 = 551 at level 29 from player_class_stats, Human race rows zero) 551 / 218 = 2.52752. A Target Dummy (4071, summon properties 61, creature 2673) the Warlock summons inside is its guardian and reports the Warlock's ratio. A level 29 Orc Warrior completes the faction pairing. Leaving through the leave packet resummons the Imp without the lift.",
